  - m_Id: 1128996235718656
    m_Localized: RAILWAY OPERATIONS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078784
    m_Localized: MY STORY
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078785
    m_Localized: 'Auto: on'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078786
    m_Localized: 'Auto: off'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078787
    m_Localized: "Skip \xB7 Start"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078788
    m_Localized: "Continue  \u203A"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078789
    m_Localized: 'Space / Enter / A: reveal text or continue     Start: skip introduction'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078790
    m_Localized: A LANDING WITH NO WAY BACK
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078791
    m_Localized: WHAT THEY TOOK FROM ME
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078792
    m_Localized: OUT OF THE RING
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078793
    m_Localized: A LIFE ON RAILS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078794
    m_Localized: THE OFFER
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078795
    m_Localized: TRAIN RANKING
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078796
    m_Localized: "I arrived on this planet eighty years ago. Yes, eighty. That isn't
      so long for a mecha witch\u2026 though it's starting to feel like an eternity."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078797
    m_Localized: 'My home was far away. I landed expecting a quick stop: refuel,
      take a look around, then return to the other mecha witches. How naive I was.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078798
    m_Localized: The World Government confiscated my ship. For security reasons,
      they said. They always say that right before taking something that doesn't
      belong to them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078799
    m_Localized: 'My star chart was aboard that ship: my only route home. With no
      ship and no map, my grand journey became a stay with no end in sight.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078800
    m_Localized: I had to make a living. I had strength, quick reflexes, and very
      little patience for orders. So I became a professional wrestler. A glamorous
      title for hitting people for a living.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078801
    m_Localized: "For a while, it worked. Applause, matches, championship belts\u2026
      and enough punches to forget government paperwork. But years passed, audiences
      changed, and eventually that profession disappeared."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078802
    m_Localized: Memories don't pay the bills. I found the best-paying job around
      and traded the ring for a cab. I became a train driver.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078803
    m_Localized: 'A simple life: pick up cargo, follow the rails, deliver on time.
      I was good at it. Apparently too good, because one day a man dressed in black
      showed up.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078804
    m_Localized: First he praised my transport skills. Then he produced an invitation
      to the Train Ranking. When someone from the government starts with compliments,
      you'd better look for the hidden catch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078805
    m_Localized: "They advertised it as the planet's greatest competition: the best
      drivers, fame, money\u2026 and a special reward. The winner could ask the World
      Government for anything."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078806
    m_Localized: Anything. My ship. My map. The way back to my home among the mecha
      witches. For the first time in eighty years, going home was more than an impossible
      dream.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078807
    m_Localized: Of course, the Train Ranking was another government scam. Aliens
      were attacking us, and they needed someone to haul a rock to their base and
      throw it at them to win the war.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078808
    m_Localized: "Sounds ridiculous. But it's not like I need a perfect shot down
      a ventilation duct and space-monk powers to pull this off. A rock should do
      the trick\u2026 according to them."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078809
    m_Localized: Getting there is the problem. Those stupid aliens have robots, machines,
      and absolutely no respect for railway schedules. And they won't be the only
      ones trying to stop me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078810
    m_Localized: The other drivers want to win too. They'll do anything to reach
      the base first and fling that rock at the aliens. At this point, I almost miss
      my old rivals in the ring.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1128996265078811
    m_Localized: "It's going to be a rough ride. But if my ship waits at the end
      of these rails, it's worth a shot. All right\u2026 cargo secured, hands on
      the controls. Time to go home."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
